/**
\fn undefined Sprite::deserialize(Deserializer deserializer)
\brief Restore selected state from a Sprite record.
\param deserializer Reader positioned at a raw Sprite record.
An initial record supplies its state flags, frame artwork and playback cursor.
It replaces existing frame images and collision masks, retaining shared resources.
Independent and authored Parts restore their IDs/names, parent/binding links,
artwork, animation tracks and bodies. Imported assets, clip/transition state,
retained Drawing artwork and built-in rig IK are restored before their dependents. Previously retained Parts are detached when replaced; IDs removed
before saving are not reused.
Incremental updates use the destination layer's serialization flags. Resource
resolution, validation or unsupported-format failures throw; discard the reader
and destination after a failed load. This operation is not an atomic scene load.
\sa Sprite::serialize(), Serializer::setResourceMode()
*/
